 "text": "When something breaks, our first thought is often to buy a new one. Yet many common problems are easy to fix. A loose chair can be tightened with a screwdriver. A dripping tap often needs only a new washer. A torn bag can be sewn in a few minutes. There are clear guides and videos for almost every repair. I keep a small box of tools at home, with glue, tape and spare screws. Fixing things saves money and reduces waste. It also gives a quiet sense of achievement. Start with something small, and build from there. Each repair teaches a new skill that will be useful again in the future."
